{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2406","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2406","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2406\",\"parent_revision\":\"a6a1effb42519a7fe5354a7283f541cc26431d602c3cd6fe519ee43f32c05833\",\"root_revision\":\"a6a1effb42519a7fe5354a7283f541cc26431d602c3cd6fe519ee43f32c05833\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID has different values in MCP server vs Bash subprocesses in remote execution\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n- Source: Issue body states verification via `/proc/638/environ` (MCP server PID) vs `echo $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` in Bash\\n- Evidence: Issue explicitly documents the split \u2014 MCP server gets `cse_...` format; Bash subprocesses get UUID format\\n- Verified by: Explicit testing of process environment tables in remote execution environment\\n\\n### Claim 2: get-gate-token.mjs runs as Bash subprocess and writes token to ~/.dh/sessions/{bash_session_id}/.gate-token\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs lines 7-21\\n- Evidence: Line 7 reads `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` from environment; lines 13-16 construct path using that session_id; lines 19-21 write token to that path\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-22\\n\\n### Claim 3: MCP server's _read_gate_token() reads from ~/.dh/sessions/{mcp_session_id}/.gate-token\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py lines 1140-1160\\n- Evidence: Line 1151 reads session_id from environment; lines 1155-1156 construct token_path as `dh_root / \\\"sessions\\\" / session_id / \\\".gate-token\\\"`; line 1158 reads from that path\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-22\\n\\n### Claim 4: _read_gate_token() is in plugins/dev